          "type": "send message",
          "content": "You have attempted this same task before and did not succeed. These are the plans you wrote after those attempts.\nTrial #1: New plan: I got stuck in a loop between the Kitchen and the Guest room, repeatedly going east and then west. What is worse, after going back and forth for some time, I decided to continue exploring new rooms instead of checking if I had already visited all the rooms. Next time, I will keep track of the rooms I have visited and check if I have already been to a room before making a move. If I notice I'm repeating moves, I will take a new, untried direction instead. I will also make sure to explore the rooms I have already visited more thoroughly before moving on to new ones.\n\nTrial #2: New plan: I got stuck in a loop between the Kitchen and the Guest room, repeatedly going east and then west, and also between the Utility room and the Sunroom, repeatedly going east and then west. What is worse, after going back and forth for some time, I decided to continue exploring new rooms instead of checking if I had already visited all the rooms. Next time, I will keep track of the rooms I have visited and check if I have already been to a room before making a move. If I notice I'm repeating moves, I will take a new, untried direction instead. I will also make sure to explore the rooms I have already visited more thoroughly before moving on to new ones. Additionally, I will pay closer attention to the available directions in each room and try to find a path that minimizes backtracking.\n\nTrial #3: New plan: I got stuck in a loop between multiple rooms, repeatedly going back and forth between them. What is worse, after going back and forth for some time, I decided to continue exploring new rooms instead of checking if I had already visited all the rooms. Next time, I will keep track of the rooms I have visited and check if I have already been to a room before making a move. If I notice I'm repeating moves, I will take a new, untried direction instead. I will also make sure to explore the rooms I have already visited more thoroughly before moving on to new ones. Additionally, I will pay closer attention to the available directions in each room and try to find a path that minimizes backtracking. Furthermore, I will make sure to explore the rooms that are directly connected to the current room before moving on to new ones. This will help me to avoid getting stuck in loops and ensure that I visit all the rooms with the fewest number of room changes possible.\n\n\nPlease help me with the following task. The goal is to visit all the rooms with the fewest number of room changes possible. In each room, you need to decide the direction to go in. Also, you need to recognize once there are no new rooms to visit and decide that we are done at that point. Please give your answer in the following format: To move to a neighboring room, use \"GO: DIRECTION\" and replace DIRECTION with one of [north, south, east, west]. To stop the exploration, answer with \"DONE\" instead. Omit any other text.\nHere is an example:\nYou are in the Kitchen. Currently available directions: south, west. What is your next instruction?\nGO: west\nYou have made a step and entered a Lobby. Currently available directions: east, north. What is your next instruction?\nGO: north\n...\nYou have made a step and entered a Bedroom. Currently available directions: south. What is your next instruction?\nDONE\nLet us start. You are in the Sunroom. Currently available directions: north, south, west. What is your next instruction?",
